    "id": 3451200,
    "postDate": "2026-05-01T01:38:50.833Z",
    "rawMarkdown": "## Tire compound changes during a race\n\n\"A tire compound refers to the specific chemical recipe of rubber, silica, carbon black, and oils used to create a tire. These compounds determine the tire's \"personality\"—balancing grip, durability, and temperature resistance.\"\n\n\"Encoded system of Tire compounds, ranging from C0 to C6 (as of 2025/2026), where 'C' stands for Compound.\n\nC0/C1 (Hardest): Most durable, best for high-abrasion tracks and high heat.\n\n\"C3 (Medium/Mid-range): The \"workhorse\" or middle-range compound, offering a balance of speed and durability.\n\nC5/C6 (Softest): Fastest over a single lap, maximum grip, but wears out very quickly (high degradation).\"\n\nColor Codes: Red (Soft), Yellow (Medium), White (Hard), Green (Intermediate), Blue (Wet).\"\n\nhttps://www.redbull.com/us-en/formula-1-tire-compounds-guide",
    "content": "<h2>Tire compound changes during a race</h2>\n<p>\"A tire compound refers to the specific chemical recipe of rubber, silica, carbon black, and oils used to create a tire. These compounds determine the tire's \"personality\"—balancing grip, durability, and temperature resistance.\"</p>\n<p>\"Encoded system of Tire compounds, ranging from C0 to C6 (as of 2025/2026), where 'C' stands for Compound.</p>\n<p>C0/C1 (Hardest): Most durable, best for high-abrasion tracks and high heat.</p>\n<p>\"C3 (Medium/Mid-range): The \"workhorse\" or middle-range compound, offering a balance of speed and durability.</p>\n<p>C5/C6 (Softest): Fastest over a single lap, maximum grip, but wears out very quickly (high degradation).\"</p>\n<p>Color Codes: Red (Soft), Yellow (Medium), White (Hard), Green (Intermediate), Blue (Wet).\"</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.redbull.com/us-en/formula-1-tire-compounds-guide\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.redbull.com/us-en/formula-1-tire-compounds-guide</a></p>",
    "parent": {
      "url": "#"
